1
00:00:00,459 --> 00:00:02,001
Oh, my God.

2
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:02,962
I know.

3
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:05,046
Monica's going
to have a baby.

4
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:07,132
Hey, can this count
as her "something new"?

5
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,302
Oh, my God.

6
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:17,267
Hey, do you think this is why
Chandler took off?

7
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:19,144
No, she had to have
just taken that test

8
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:20,980
because I took out the trash
last night.

9
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,649
Oh, God, this is turning
into the worst wedding day ever.

10
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:26,067
The bride is pregnant,
the groom is missing

11
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:27,653
and I'm still
holding this.

12
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:34,034
Okay, Phoebe, we cannot
tell anyone about this.

13
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:35,870
Okay?
Right. Yeah, okay.

14
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:37,496
Hey, wait.

15
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:40,165
Do you know what kind
of birth control
she was using?

16
00:00:40,207 --> 00:00:41,333
No. Why?

17
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:42,668
Just for the future.

18
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,294
This is hardly
a commercial for it.

19
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,513
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

20
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:55,931
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

21
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:59,727
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

22
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:05,190
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

23
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:08,777
Anything?

24
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:10,612
No. I talked to Joey
on the set.

25
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:12,197
He hasn't heard
from him.

26
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:14,658
I talked to Chandler's
parents again.

27
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,159
You told them
he was missing?

28
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:19,413
No. I made it seem like
I was just calling to chat.

29
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,331
I'm pretty sure
they both think

30
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:22,833
I'm interested in them.

31
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:24,752
All right, we've
got to tell her
that he's gone.

32
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:26,169
No, hey, hey, we can't.

33
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,838
She's going to start
getting ready soon.

34
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,715
Can't you at least
stall her a little?

35
00:01:29,757 --> 00:01:32,342
I'll go back to some
of the places I went last night.

36
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:33,844
Well, how much
time do you need?

37
00:01:33,886 --> 00:01:35,220
How much time before

38
00:01:35,262 --> 00:01:36,847
she absolutely has
to start getting ready?

39
00:01:36,889 --> 00:01:37,723
One hour.

40
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:38,557
Give me two.

41
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:39,767
Then why do you ask?

42
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,728
Okay, wish me luck.

43
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:44,688
Okay. I'm going
with you.

44
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:46,440
Why?

45
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,482
Ross, you're tired.

46
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:49,026
You've been
looking all night

47
00:01:49,068 --> 00:01:50,736
and clearly,
you suck at this.

48
00:01:51,987 --> 00:01:53,321
I'll see
you guys later.

49
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,032
Do you know how
you're going to stall her?

50
00:01:55,074 --> 00:01:56,951
I'll figure something out.

51
00:01:56,992 --> 00:01:58,827
All right, good luck.

52
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:00,871
Hey.

53
00:02:00,913 --> 00:02:02,456
Okay, so I thought
we'd start

54
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:04,374
with my makeup
and then do my hair.

55
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:06,585
Okay, uh, but before
you do that

56
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:08,462
I-I need you
to talk to me.

57
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:09,546
About what?

58
00:02:09,588 --> 00:02:12,299
Um...

59
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:16,553
( voice breaking ):
I'm never going
to get married.

60
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:17,930
Yeah, you will.

61
00:02:17,972 --> 00:02:19,807
The right guy's just
around the corner.

62
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,349
Okay, are we done with that?

63
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,770
No, Monica,
I'm serious.

64
00:02:24,812 --> 00:02:27,856
Oh, maybe I should just
forget about it.

65
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:30,191
Become a lesbian
or something.

66
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:32,611
Any woman would be
lucky to have you.

67
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,657
Well, maybe it would
make me feel better

68
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:37,908
if I slept with Joey.

69
00:02:37,950 --> 00:02:40,077
Rachel, are you okay?

70
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:46,125
Excuse me, Aaron?

71
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,417
Hi. Um...

72
00:02:47,459 --> 00:02:49,294
I have a little problem
with the schedule.

73
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:51,630
See, originally, I wasn't
supposed to work today

74
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:54,716
and I have this wedding
that I really have to be at.

75
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:57,094
It's my best friend's
and I'm officiating

76
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:59,346
so I really can't
work past 4:00.

77
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:01,389
Joey, you've
got to stay
until the end.

78
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,308
We can't stop filming
just for you.

79
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:05,102
It's not like
it's your wedding.

80
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:08,981
I'm having surgery.

81
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,566
What?

82
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:14,111
Yeah, I just made up
the stuff about the wedding

83
00:03:14,153 --> 00:03:16,530
because I didn't want
you to worry about me.

84
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,157
But I'm having
surgery today.

85
00:03:18,197 --> 00:03:19,992
What kind of surgery?

86
00:03:20,034 --> 00:03:24,038
Transplant.

87
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:26,790
But you're supposed
to work on Monday.

88
00:03:26,832 --> 00:03:30,044
Hair transplant.

89
00:03:30,085 --> 00:03:31,795
But you're not bald.

90
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:34,923
It's not on my head.

91
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:40,012
Look, Joey, there's
nothing I can do.

92
00:03:40,054 --> 00:03:43,222
Besides, you're
probably going to be
out by 4:00 anyway.

93
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,017
We've just got
one short scene.

94
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:47,061
It's just you
and Richard

95
00:03:47,102 --> 00:03:49,063
and God knows
he's a pro.

96
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:50,397
You'll be fine.

97
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:51,606
Morning, Richard.

98
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:52,733
Hey, you're here.

99
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,068
Great, great, great.

100
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:55,402
Let's get going, buddy.

101
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:57,071
We've got a scene
to shoot.

102
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:01,491
I'm wearing two belts.

103
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:05,954
Are you drunk?

104
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:07,039
No.

105
00:04:07,081 --> 00:04:08,248
Yes, you are.

106
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:10,125
All right.

107
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,423
So this is your office.

108
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:17,674
How did you guys
find me?

109
00:04:17,716 --> 00:04:20,969
I knew I should have
hid at the gym.

110
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:22,930
What the hell
are you doing?

111
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:24,431
Panicking...

112
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:26,934
and using the Internet
to try to prove

113
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:28,810
that I'm related to Monica.

114
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:31,772
How is she?

115
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:32,773
ROSS:
She's fine.

116
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,108
She doesn't know
you're gone.

117
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:36,193
And she doesn't
have to know, okay?

118
00:04:36,235 --> 00:04:37,986
Now come on,
we're going home.

119
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:39,571
No, no, I can't do that.

120
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:40,572
Why not?

121
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:42,116
Because if I go home

122
00:04:42,157 --> 00:04:44,284
we're going to become the Bings.

123
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,911
I can't be the Bings.

124
00:04:45,953 --> 00:04:47,579
What's wrong with
being the Bings?

125
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:49,915
The Bings have
horrible marriages.

126
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:51,625
They yell, they fight

127
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:55,254
and they use the pool boy
as a pawn in their sexual games.

128
00:04:55,294 --> 00:04:58,715
Chandler, have
you ever put on a
black cocktail dress

129
00:04:58,757 --> 00:05:01,093
and asked me up
to your hotel room?

130
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:02,261
No.

131
00:05:02,301 --> 00:05:04,679
Then you are neither
of your parents.

132
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,349
It's not just
their marriage.

133
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,768
I mean, look at yours.

134
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:11,186
Look at everybody's.

135
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:13,647
The only person
that can make
marriage work

136
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:15,065
is Paul Newman.

137
00:05:15,107 --> 00:05:17,567
And I have met me--
I am no Paul Newman.

138
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,486
I don't race cars,
I don't make popcorn.

139
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:21,155
None of my proceeds
go to charity.

140
00:05:21,196 --> 00:05:24,365
But look, Chandler

141
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:27,744
right now, no one has
a lower opinion

142
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:29,454
of you than I do.

143
00:05:31,165 --> 00:05:33,917
But I totally believe
you can do this.

144
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:35,627
I want to.

145
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:37,212
I love her so much.

146
00:05:37,254 --> 00:05:38,505
But I'm afra...

147
00:05:38,546 --> 00:05:39,798
This is too huge.

148
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,758
You know, okay,
you're right

149
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,302
it is huge.

150
00:05:43,342 --> 00:05:45,971
So why don't we take
it just a little
bit at a time.

151
00:05:46,013 --> 00:05:48,223
Okay, forget
getting married
for a second.

152
00:05:48,265 --> 00:05:50,184
Just forget about it.

153
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:53,854
Can you just come home
and take a shower?

154
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,939
That's not
scary, right?

155
00:05:55,981 --> 00:05:57,858
Depends on what you mean
by "we."

156
00:05:57,899 --> 00:06:00,485
Okay.

157
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:04,031
The nights
are the hardest.

158
00:06:05,406 --> 00:06:07,034
But then the day comes

159
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:10,369
and that's every bit
as hard as the night.

160
00:06:12,039 --> 00:06:13,665
And then the night comes again.

161
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,876
The days and nights are hard,
I get it, okay?

162
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:17,085
Look, Rachel, I'm sorry.

163
00:06:17,127 --> 00:06:18,586
I have to start getting ready.

164
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:19,880
I'm getting married today.

165
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,673
I know.

166
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,300
At dusk.

167
00:06:23,342 --> 00:06:25,510
That's such a hard time for me.

168
00:06:25,552 --> 00:06:26,678
Okay.

169
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,180
I'm going to go
put my makeup on.

170
00:06:28,222 --> 00:06:29,848
We have to be at the
hotel in an hour.

171
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,183
Okay. Wait.

172
00:06:31,225 --> 00:06:32,184
What?

173
00:06:32,226 --> 00:06:34,561
Let's go to lunch.

174
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:36,521
I can't go to lunch!

175
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,273
Right.

176
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:43,237
Oh, good God, I've fallen down!

177
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,907
What's going on?

178
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:50,118
Okay.

179
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,037
All right, honey, listen.

180
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:56,291
When I tell you what
I'm about to tell you

181
00:06:56,333 --> 00:07:00,128
I need you to remember
that we are all here for you

182
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:01,713
and that we love you.

183
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:04,216
Okay, you're really
freaking me out.

184
00:07:04,258 --> 00:07:08,469
We can't find Chandler.

185
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:11,723
...s vest.

186
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:14,268
We can't find Chandler's vest.

187
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:15,269
How can that be?

188
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:16,603
Wait, are you serious?

189
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:20,065
Found the vest.

190
00:07:20,107 --> 00:07:21,983
I mean, we're going to have
to keep an eye on it.

191
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:23,693
You know, make sure
we don't lose it again.

192
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:25,237
Oh.

193
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:26,238
Oh, well, okay.

194
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,198
Don't scare me like that, okay?

195
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,950
I mean, for
a minute there

196
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:33,787
I was like, Oh, my God,
the worst has happened.

197
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:34,829
Oh, whoo!

198
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:49,844
So-so, you two
were married, huh?

199
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:54,433
What happened,
you just drift apart?

200
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,145
Here comes the bride.

201
00:07:58,186 --> 00:07:59,313
Oh.

202
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:00,521
( gasps )

203
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:03,608
Oh, my God, Monica!

204
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,026
( gasping )

205
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:07,446
I want to wear
this every day.

206
00:08:07,486 --> 00:08:09,697
You look so beautiful.

207
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:12,826
I'm so happy for me.

208
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:15,245
( phone rings )

209
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:17,747
Hello.

210
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:19,874
Hey. Did Chandler show up yet?

211
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:21,460
Yeah. We got him back;
everything's fine.

212
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,586
Damn it!

213
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:25,297
What? Why? Where are you?

214
00:08:25,339 --> 00:08:27,466
I'm still on the set.

215
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,634
Joey, the wedding is
in less than an hour.

216
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,011
I know. I'm sorry.

217
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:32,387
The guy's drunk.

218
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,639
They won't let me go
until we get this.

219
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:36,141
Oh, my God.

220
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:38,435
I'm going to have to find
another minister.

221
00:08:38,477 --> 00:08:40,437
No! No, I'm the minister.

222
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:43,357
All right, look, look,
put them both on the phone.

223
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:44,941
I'll marry them right now.

224
00:08:44,983 --> 00:08:47,235
Oh! Joey, I have to go.

225
00:08:47,277 --> 00:08:48,903
Hey, don't you hang up on me.

226
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,072
I'll marry you and me
right now-- I have the power.

227
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,119
There you go.

228
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:58,455
You put on a tuxedo.

229
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:01,041
Now, that wasn't
so scary, was it?

230
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,626
No.

231
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:06,963
I'm telling you, just
a little bit at a time.

232
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:09,341
Yeah, okay, wh-what's
the next little bit?

233
00:09:09,383 --> 00:09:11,218
Getting married.

234
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,344
( gasps )

235
00:09:12,386 --> 00:09:13,720
Okay, okay,
but you can...

236
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:15,096
you can do that, too.

237
00:09:15,138 --> 00:09:17,598
just like you've
done everything else.

238
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:20,560
Yeah, you're right.

239
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:21,895
I... I-I can do that.

240
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:23,230
Yeah.

241
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:25,440
Okay, excuse me
for a minute.

242
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,067
Where... where are you going?

243
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:29,069
Ross, I'm not going
to run away again.

244
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:31,154
I just want to get
a little fresh air.

245
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:33,031
Okay.
Okay.

246
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:43,791
Oh, fresh air.

247
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,420
RACHEL:
Okay, Phoebe, you're going
to have to cover for me.

248
00:09:46,461 --> 00:09:48,588
PHOEBE:
Wait. Maybe, maybe
you're overreacting.

249
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:49,964
You do that, you know?

250
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:51,632
Oh. Well, Phoebe,
we got to do something.

251
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:53,134
You know? I mean,
there's no way

252
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:54,593
Joey's going to
make it in time

253
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:55,970
so I'm going to go
through the hotel

254
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:58,181
and see if there's any
other weddings going on.

255
00:09:58,223 --> 00:10:00,434
Okay. Oh, but don't tell them
Monica's pregnant

256
00:10:00,475 --> 00:10:01,726
'cause they frown on that.

257
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:03,103
Okay.

258
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,187
Okay.

259
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:18,076
"Anastassakis
Papasifakis wedding."

260
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:19,327
Excellent.

261
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,622
Congratulations.

262
00:10:23,664 --> 00:10:25,250
Mazel tov.

263
00:10:25,292 --> 00:10:26,585
Hi. Oh, great hat.

264
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:27,919
Come here.

265
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:31,714
Listen, I need you to
perform another wedding.

266
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,007
Can you do that?

267
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:34,468
I don't know.

268
00:10:34,509 --> 00:10:36,136
Are they Greek Orthodox?

269
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:37,762
Yeah, yeah, they're...

270
00:10:37,804 --> 00:10:42,350
They're my friends, uh,
Monica Stephanopolous

271
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:47,105
and, uh... and
Chandler... Acidophilus.

272
00:10:51,485 --> 00:10:53,027
Hi.

273
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,237
Hi.

274
00:10:55,572 --> 00:10:57,365
Hi.

275
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:02,120
Has, um, anyone
seen Chandler?

276
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,288
I thought he
was with you.

277
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:05,248
He was with me.

278
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:08,293
Um, we're playing a little game;
you know, hide-and-seek.

279
00:11:08,335 --> 00:11:10,128
You can't ask us, son.

280
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:11,921
That's cheating.

281
00:11:15,425 --> 00:11:17,051
You're right.

282
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:19,929
Thanks for keeping me honest,
Dad.

283
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:22,056
Well, he better not
come by here.

284
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,891
He can't see the bride
in her wedding dress.

285
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:25,893
As I recall,
when we got married

286
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:28,396
I saw the groom
in the wedding dress.

287
00:11:28,438 --> 00:11:30,731
That was after the wedding.

288
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:32,733
It's not bad luck then.

289
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:35,111
Honey, it isn't good luck.

290
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:41,368
Oh, my God!

291
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:42,494
Monica!

292
00:11:42,536 --> 00:11:44,412
I know.

293
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:46,747
Hey, how's Chandler doing?

294
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:47,457
Great.

295
00:11:47,499 --> 00:11:49,376
He's doing great.

296
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:52,920
Don't you worry
about Chandler.

297
00:11:54,339 --> 00:11:56,508
Uh, Phoebe, can I
see you for a second?

298
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:57,467
Yeah.

299
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:04,599
What's going on?

300
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:05,808
Chandler's gone again.

301
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,310
Oh, my God!

302
00:12:07,352 --> 00:12:09,354
Why would you play
hide-and-seek with someone

303
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:11,648
you know is a flight risk?

304
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:17,736
Aaron, you got
to let me go.

305
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:18,988
The guy's hammered.

306
00:12:19,030 --> 00:12:20,281
I'm sorry, Joey.

307
00:12:20,323 --> 00:12:22,242
As long as he's here
and he's conscious

308
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,284
we're still shooting.

309
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:36,423
You wouldn't happen to have
a very big fork?

310
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:41,636
So I, uh, I just
talked to the director.

311
00:12:41,678 --> 00:12:42,803
That's it.

312
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:44,681
We're done for the day.

313
00:12:44,723 --> 00:12:47,267
Have we finished the scene?

314
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:49,728
Yeah, you were wonderful.

315
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,188
As were you.

316
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:53,231
So I got your car.

317
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:54,815
It's right outside.

318
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:57,818
Thank you.
You're welcome.

319
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:00,029
No, no, no,
we got to go.

320
00:13:00,071 --> 00:13:01,448
Come on.

321
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:02,907
Here we go.

322
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:05,826
Is that my ass?

323
00:13:12,751 --> 00:13:14,377
There he is!

324
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:15,378
What?

325
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,380
Hey, no!

326
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:20,174
You're not getting away
this time, mister

327
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:23,511
unless you want that ass-kicking
we talked about!

328
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:25,346
Ross!

329
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:27,056
Hi-ya!

330
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,435
I'm serious.

331
00:13:30,477 --> 00:13:32,811
You're not walking out
on my sister.

332
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,272
That's right; I'm not.

333
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:36,441
Then where the hell
have you been?

334
00:13:36,483 --> 00:13:38,735
I know about Monica.

335
00:13:38,777 --> 00:13:40,111
You know?

336
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:41,904
What?

337
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:43,698
I heard you
and Rachel talking.

338
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,325
What, what,
talking about what?

339
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:46,867
You don't know?

340
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:50,288
If someone doesn't tell me
what's going on right now...

341
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,332
What, you'll "hi-ya"?

342
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:56,169
Monica's pregnant.

343
00:13:58,004 --> 00:13:59,506
Oh, my God.

344
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:01,800
Oh, my God!

345
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,677
And you're not...
you're not freaking out?

346
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:04,927
Well, I was.

347
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:06,763
Then I went down
to the gift shop

348
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:07,888
'cause I was out of cigarettes.

349
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:08,807
Cigarettes?!

350
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:11,351
Big picture, please.

351
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:13,978
So when I was
in the gift shop

352
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,313
that's when I, uh...

353
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:17,607
saw this.

354
00:14:19,442 --> 00:14:20,901
And I thought

355
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:23,363
anything that can fit into this
can't be scary.

356
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:27,492
You obviously didn't see
Chucky III.

357
00:14:27,534 --> 00:14:29,035
No, but come on.

358
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:31,621
Look how cute and small this is.

359
00:14:31,663 --> 00:14:36,584
So I got it to give Monica
so she'd... know I was okay.

360
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:38,753
Dude.

361
00:14:38,795 --> 00:14:40,129
Way to go, son.

362
00:14:40,171 --> 00:14:41,673
I knew you'd find him.

363
00:14:49,681 --> 00:14:53,184
Our little boy
is getting married.

364
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:54,561
Oh, look at you.

365
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,103
So handsome.

366
00:14:56,145 --> 00:14:58,356
You look beautiful, Mom.

367
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,024
( clears throat )

368
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:04,320
You look beautiful, too, Dad.

369
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:09,367
I love you both.

370
00:15:09,409 --> 00:15:11,870
I'm so glad you're here.

371
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:19,544
Are you Chandler?

372
00:15:19,586 --> 00:15:21,920
Are you Joey?

373
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:28,845
Huh, this is nice.

374
00:15:28,887 --> 00:15:30,805
What?

375
00:15:30,847 --> 00:15:36,394
I've never walked down the aisle
knowing it can't end in divorce.

376
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,825
( sighs )

377
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:53,536
I wish your grandmother
had lived to see this.

378
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:55,371
She's right there.

379
00:15:55,413 --> 00:15:57,123
Not that
old crone.

380
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:58,583
My mother.

381
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,839
Congratulations,
darling.

382
00:16:04,881 --> 00:16:06,424
We love you,
sweetheart.

383
00:16:10,762 --> 00:16:11,721
You look beautiful.

384
00:16:11,763 --> 00:16:13,556
Is this new?

385
00:16:13,598 --> 00:16:14,641
Not now.

386
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:16,350
Okay.

387
00:16:20,772 --> 00:16:21,940
Who is this?

388
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,190
I am Father Karamessos.

389
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:25,192
He's Greek Orthodox.

390
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:27,779
As are you.

391
00:16:29,948 --> 00:16:31,616
Let us begin.

392
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:33,992
Dearly beloved...

393
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:35,453
That's my line.

394
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:43,503
I can take it
from here, thanks.

395
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:49,467
Dearly beloved,
I'm sorry I'm a little late.

396
00:16:51,845 --> 00:16:54,681
You may be confused by this now

397
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:58,852
but you won't be
Memorial Day weekend, 2002.

398
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:04,732
Well, let's get started before
the groom takes off again, huh?

399
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:14,701
We are gathered here today

400
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:22,040
to join this man and this woman
in the bonds of holy matrimony.

401
00:17:22,082 --> 00:17:25,085
I've known Monica and Chandler
for a long time

402
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:31,759
and I cannot imagine two people
more perfect for each other.

403
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:35,221
And now...

404
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:38,808
as I've left my notes
in my dressing room

405
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:41,686
we shall proceed to the vows.

406
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:42,729
Monica.

407
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:45,690
He took off?

408
00:17:45,732 --> 00:17:47,734
Go on, go on.

409
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:57,284
Chandler, for so long, I...

410
00:17:57,326 --> 00:18:01,372
I wondered if I would
ever find my prince.

411
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:03,791
My soul mate.

412
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:06,460
Then three years ago,
at another wedding

413
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:09,129
I turned to a friend
for comfort

414
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:11,382
and instead

415
00:18:11,424 --> 00:18:14,719
I found everything that I'd
ever been looking for

416
00:18:14,761 --> 00:18:16,387
my whole life.

417
00:18:17,847 --> 00:18:25,354
And now, here we are,
with our future before us...

418
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:30,359
and I only want to
spend it with you.

419
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:37,075
My prince, my soul mate,
my friend.

420
00:18:40,411 --> 00:18:42,246
Unless you don't want to.

421
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:46,709
You go.

422
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,378
Chandler.

423
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:51,798
Uh, that's okay.

424
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:58,888
Monica, I thought this
was going to be

425
00:18:58,930 --> 00:19:01,682
the most difficult thing
I ever had to do.

426
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:04,769
But when I saw you
walking down that aisle

427
00:19:04,811 --> 00:19:07,730
I realized how
simple it was.

428
00:19:09,816 --> 00:19:11,525
I love you.

429
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:15,237
Any surprises that
come our way

430
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:18,365
it's okay, because
I will always love you.

431
00:19:20,076 --> 00:19:21,410
You are the person

432
00:19:21,452 --> 00:19:24,163
I was meant to spend
the rest of my life with.

433
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:27,708
You want to know
if I'm sure?

434
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:34,007
You may now
kiss the bride.

435
00:19:35,925 --> 00:19:37,468
So...

436
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:40,680
I guess by the powers
vested in me

437
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:44,058
by the state of New York
and the Internet guys...

438
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:50,857
I now pronounce you
husband and wife.

439
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:51,691
Oh, wait.

440
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,860
Do you take each other?

441
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,277
I do.

442
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:56,362
I do.

443
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:58,114
Yeah, you do.

444
00:19:58,990 --> 00:20:00,700
Rings.

445
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,702
Oh, crap. Okay, um...

446
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,245
Let's do the rings.

447
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:19,301
We good?

448
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:20,845
Okay.

449
00:20:20,887 --> 00:20:26,392
Once again, I pronounce you
husband and wife.

450
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:28,310
Kiss her again.

451
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:45,953
I love you.

452
00:20:45,995 --> 00:20:48,414
And I know about the baby.

453
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:50,249
What baby?

454
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:51,333
Our baby.

455
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:53,335
We have a baby?

456
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:57,297
Phoebe found your pregnancy test
in the trash.

457
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:59,759
I didn't take
a pregnancy test.

458
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,761
Then who did?

459
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:03,846
Look at them.

460
00:21:03,888 --> 00:21:07,474
Oh, and they're
going to have a baby.

461
00:21:09,102 --> 00:21:11,437
Uh-huh.

